## 2. Open Policy Agent (OPA) Guardrails
To prevent automated agents from executing destructive cluster commands or exfiltrating sensitive credentials, we introduce an OPA validation gate at the **Model Context Protocol (MCP)** execution tier.

### Rego Policy Definition
Save this policy file as `llm-tool-guardrails.rego`. It enforces a strict blacklist of forbidden infrastructure operations and enforces data minimization rules on incoming payloads.

```rego
package llm.mesh.authz

# Deny by default
default allow = false

# Allow the tool execution only if it passes all safety criteria
allow {
    not tool_is_blacklisted
    not payload_contains_secrets
    request_origin_verified
}

# 1. Blacklist destructive infrastructure verbs
tool_is_blacklisted {
    forbidden_verbs := {"delete", "patch", "update", "exec", "destroy"}
    some verb in forbidden_verbs
    contains(lower(input.tool_arguments.command), verb)
}

# 2. Block scanning for core infrastructure secrets/tokens
payload_contains_secrets {
    forbidden_resources := {"secret", "token", "kubeconfig", "password", "tls.key"}
    some resource in forbidden_resources
    contains(lower(input.tool_arguments.target), resource)
}

# 3. Enforce that requests must originate from trusted mesh namespaces
request_origin_verified {
    trusted_namespaces := {"agent-mesh", "ai-analytics"}
    trusted_namespaces[input.mesh_metadata.source_namespace]
}

# Construct structured diagnostic message for Kagent trace logs
deny_reason[msg] {
    tool_is_blacklisted
    msg := sprintf("Security Exception: Tool execution rejected. The command contains a forbidden destructive verb.", [])
}

deny_reason[msg] {
    payload_contains_secrets
    msg := sprintf("Security Exception: Data Access Denied. The target footprint requests sensitive infrastructure secrets.", [])
}
```

